# Quality gates (required on every change)

Before finishing any implementation in this repo, you **must** satisfy all of the following.

## 1. Tests

- Place tests in `__tests__/` next to the code under test.
- **Unit tests:** `*.unit.test.ts` — pure logic, no live DB/network.
- **Integration tests:** `*.integration.test.ts` — SQLite, filesystem, or multi-module flows.
- **E2E tests:** `*.e2e.test.tsx` — full `<App />` flows with `ink-testing-library`.
- When you **add, change, or remove** behavior, **add, update, or remove** the matching tests in the same change.
- Coverage threshold is **80%** on gated paths (`src/core`, `src/config`, `src/theme`). Run `pnpm test:coverage` locally.

```bash
pnpm unitary:test
pnpm integration:test
pnpm e2e:test
```

## 2. Documentation

- Keep `/docs` accurate when features, architecture, or public behavior change.
- Update the relevant file under `docs/features/`, `docs/components/`, or `docs/architecture.md`.
- If you add a screen or core service, document it in the matching doc page.

## 3. Static checks (all must pass)

```bash
pnpm format:check   # Prettier
pnpm lint:check     # ESLint
pnpm types:check    # TypeScript
```

Or run the full gate:

```bash
pnpm quality
# or: pnpm nx run helm-cli:quality
```

## 4. Do not skip gates

- Do not commit with failing lint, format, typecheck, or tests.
- Do not disable coverage thresholds or ESLint rules to “make CI green” without explicit user approval.
- UI-only work still requires passing static checks; add tests when logic in `core/` or shared components changes.

## 5. Helm conventions still apply

Follow `helm-conventions.mdc` (ESM `.js` imports, no `import React`, tokens from `theme/theme.ts`, paths via `config/paths.ts`).
